From 49c0b629fa59612f1242fbb72f31b2e113f78901 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vrisan Shah <vrisan@example.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 20:30:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Extend writing contests with stages/scoring/judging + AI
 reading competition creator
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Applies on top of the avatar-customization-v2 commit — apply that patch
first if you haven't yet.

- New migration 034: adds stage/score/admin_feedback to the EXISTING
  writing_submissions table (migration 024) instead of creating a
  parallel writing_contests table. Also adds tagline to the existing
  challenges table for the AI reading-competition formatter.
- Writing contest advancement (Participant -> Semifinalist -> Finalist ->
  Top 3) is additive alongside the existing official/community winner
  flow in app/api/competitions/[id]/judge — that route is untouched.
- New admin judging pipeline: app/admin/writing-submissions (Entry
  Reader: read full submissions, score, advance stage, leave feedback)
  plus a Top 3 contact-export panel (admin-only, read-only, scoped to
  stage='top_3' submissions in one competition — never a bulk PII dump).
- New admin AI reading-competition creator: app/admin/reading-challenges.
  Admin supplies the facts (type/target/dates/notes); AI only formats
  title/description/tagline/badge — it never invents the target number.
  Inserts into the existing challenges table, not a new one.
- Student writing-contest hub redesign: card styling matches
  ChallengesClient's visual language, live countdown to submission/voting
  deadline, stage badges on entries, and a Top 3 leaderboard once a
  competition completes.
- AdminNav: added the two new admin pages.
